        "original_id": "a9669715-82ae-59ad-a86e-42f3df7d0287",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mehdi Mahdavikia\n- Organizations: Hamburger SV, Iran national football team, Persepolis, Eintracht Frankfurt, Steel Azin, Damash Gilan, Bank Melli youth academy\n- Places: Tehran, Hamburg, Germany\n- Events: 1998 FIFA World Cup\n\nFacts:\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia was born on 24 July 1977 in Tehran.\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia is a retired Iranian football player.\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia came through the Bank Melli youth academy and then joined Persepolis.\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia played in the 1998 FIFA World Cup, and his performance there led to a transfer to Hamburger SV.\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia played for Hamburger SV in the Bundesliga for eight seasons.\n- Mehdi Mahdavikia also played for Eintracht Frankfurt, Steel Azin, Damash Gilan, and the Iran national football team.\n- Hamburger SV, also known as Hamburg or HSV, is a German sport club based in Hamburg.\n- Hamburger SV's largest branch is its football department.",
